# New skill → README promo visual (required)

Whenever you **add or publish** a new skill under `skills/`, treat README marketing assets as part of the same release — not a follow-up.

## Checklist (before commit/push)

1. **Ship the skill** — `skills/<name>/SKILL.md` (+ scripts only if needed).
2. **Create a feature promo visual** for that skill (prefer `nic-visual-code`: SVG/HTML; AI bitmap only if intentionally atmospheric via `nic-image-gen`).
3. **Commit the visual under** `docs/<skill-short-name>/` or `docs/promo/` (never rely on gitignored `nic-skills-artifacts/` for README).
4. **Update `README.md`**
   - Add/update the Skills table row.
   - Add a short **Featured** (or per-skill) section: 1–3 sentence capability blurb + install snippet + example image(s).
5. **Embed with constrained width** (GitHub uses intrinsic SVG size otherwise):

```html
<img src="./docs/.../skill-promo.svg" alt="..." width="720" />
<img src="./docs/.../skill-diagram.svg" alt="..." width="640" />
<img src="./docs/.../skill-icon.svg" alt="..." width="128" />
```

Defaults: banner/promo `720`, diagram `640`, icon `128`.

## Do / Don't

| Do | Don't |
|----|--------|
| One clear promo that shows what the skill does | Ship skill with table-only README mention |
| UTF-8 / no mojibake; brand-safe paths in docs | Link README to `nic-skills-artifacts/` (ignored) |
| Keep section scannable | Dump huge unscaled SVGs |

## Reference

Existing pattern: Featured `nic-visual-code` section + `docs/visual-code/*` in `README.md`.
